# Key-driven scenario judged automatically: each `expect` compares the terminal
# with the screen `temzdf standalone pdf --render-frame` draws after the same keys, so it
# checks the path from viewer state to pixels on screen (placements, crops,
# updates, stale images), not PDF rendering itself (both sides use MuPDF).
# Used with: scripts/e2e.sh tests/e2e/expect.actions -- target/debug/temzdf standalone pdf --clean target/fixtures/sample.pdf
# Expected: every line of OUTDIR/expect.txt is PASS (the script exits 4 otherwise).
pause 1
expect start ""
# One key at a time: quick repeats accelerate scrolling (flick), which the
# headless renderer (it lets each key's animation settle) does not reproduce.
for _ in 1 2 3; do keys j; pause 0.6; done
expect scrolled "jjj"
keys plus
pause 0.3
keys plus
pause 1.5
expect zoomed "jjj++"
keys 0
pause 1
expect fit "jjj++0"
keys 2 shift+g
pause 1.5
expect page2 "jjj++02G"
# (The search, typed after /, is out until the search prompt is back:
# todo.md.)
keys Tab
pause 1
expect sidebar "jjj++02G<Tab>"
